  "description": {
    "text": "A card album made for the tenth Pokémon film, The Rise of Darkrai, holding eleven holofoil cards of the central Pokémon of the first nine films, from Striking Back Mewtwo to Prince of the Sea Manaphy. Each card's name carries a place or phrase from its film, and each has its own Pokédex entry about that film. The cards have no number, level or rarity mark, only the set's own symbol.\n\nVisitors to the World Hobby Fair could buy it early, from 14 January 2007; it then came out in cinemas on 14 July 2007 and in shops on 3 August 2007. The album has a twelfth space for the Darkrai card given to the first 4,200,000 cinema-goers, which belongs to the DP-P promos instead.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Bulbapedia: 10th Movie Commemoration Set (TCG) (Wayback Machine copy, 29 August 2026)",
        "url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20260829180734/https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/10th_Movie_Commemoration_Set_(TCG)"
      }
    ]
  },
  "tell": {
    "text": "A \"10th\" film-strip mark at the bottom right",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Pokémon Card Game 30th Anniversary Archive (The Pokémon Company): each card's expansion mark",
        "url": "https://www.30tharchive.pokemon-card.com/"
      },
      {
        "title": "Bulbapedia: 10th Movie Commemoration Set (TCG) (Wayback Machine copy, 29 August 2026)",
        "url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20260829180734/https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/10th_Movie_Commemoration_Set_(TCG)"
      }
    ]
  },
